{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5ibtis8AQeKdum3gvZC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis of the codebase:\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Endpoints use `@PostMapping`/`@GetMapping` with `@PathVariable` for resource IDs\n- Error handling via `ConflictException` (409) and `ResourceNotFoundException` (404)\n- Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses; `GlobalExceptionHandler` converts to `ApiError` responses\n- Error codes defined in `ErrorCode` enum with pattern: `ENTITY_PROBLEM` or `ENTITY_STATE`\n- Tests use `MockMvc` with `jsonPath` assertions on error responses\n- Response includes `error.code` field for machine-readable error identification\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — must add error code for the state conflict case (when confirming a cancelled shipment)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` method\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for all four cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- Modifying `ApiError.kt` changes the shared API layer, but is necessary for proper error contract compliance\n- State transition logic must handle CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→no-op (idempotent), CANCELLED→error correctly\n\n**Open questions:** None that affect behavior; error code naming will follow existing convention.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add a new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This will be used when attempting to confirm a shipment that is in the `CANCELLED` state. This follows the existing naming pattern (ENTITY_PROBLEM).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new method `confirm()` with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Takes `shipmentId` as `@PathVariable`\n   - Calls `repository.findById(shipmentId)` and throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found (404)\n   - Checks the shipment's current status:\n     - If `CREATED`: creates new shipment with `CONFIRMED` status, saves it, returns it with 200\n     - If `CONFIRMED`: returns it unchanged with 200 (idempotent)\n     - If `CANCELLED`: throws `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` code (409)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` — verifies status changes and is persisted\n   - `confirms a CONFIRMED shipment idempotently` — verifies repeated confirm succeeds\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409` — verifies conflict exception\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404` — verifies not found exception\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using `VALIDATION_FAILED` error code for cancelled shipments: This would reuse an existing code but misrepresents the error type (validation errors are for input validation, not state conflicts). The existing pattern is to have specific codes for specific state issues (e.g., `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS`), so adding `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` is consistent.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Code |\n|------|------|-------|----------|------|\n| CREATED shipment | repository.findById(id) | save with CONFIRMED | Shipment, 200 | ✓ |\n| Already CONFIRMED | repository.findById(id) | none (no-op) | Shipment, 200 | ✓ |\n| CANCELLED shipment | repository.findById(id) | none | error envelope, 409 | SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE |\n| Non-existent id | repository.findById(id) returns null | none | error envelope, 404 | SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Create shipment in CREATED, confirm it, verify status is CONFIRMED and JSON response shows it\n- Test 2: Create and confirm a shipment, confirm again, verify status remains CONFIRMED and succeeds\n- Test 3: Create shipment, write CANCELLED status directly to repository, attempt confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code\n- Test 4: Attempt confirm on non-existent id, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":413,"cache_read_input_tokens":21582,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":413},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fce4b44c-3b6d-4578-a852-4fd49f81d6a2","uuid":"9f6017df-5547-4253-b8a6-6abaa7e43eb8","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:43:36.521Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5ibtE6MbqPhhmeAwmun"}
